{
  "case_id": "2022-22-105",
  "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Coinbase, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: When a party appeals the denial of a motion to compel arbitration, it stays litigation. That result follows from the centuries-old divestiture rule, as well as by Congress's choice to adopt an asymmetric interlocutory rule in FAA Section 16(a)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Haven't we treated qualified immunity differently from other interlocutory appeals?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Well, let me be clear, and this is my final point. Does it follow automatically that when you have an interlocutory appeal, there's an automatic stay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Why is that different than a forum selection clause, which we say is not subject to an automatic stay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Coinbase, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: So -- so, Justice Sotomayor, two things. One is I don't believe you've ever said that if it's just a forum selection clause, Griggs doesn't work. You've certainly said, if it's a forum selections argument, you don't have a right to an interlocutory appeal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: Justice Jackson, my point is, if Congress doesn't think it follows that an automatic stay comes from an interlocutory appeal, they say precisely that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amici briefs",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0001-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: Right. As our brief says and the amici briefs say, we have a lot of empirical evidence on this that shows that these discretionary stays are not granted under the Nken factors and that huge harm results in the interim because discovery comes out, it spills out into the open, which is the very bargained-for thing that the arbitration agreement was all about."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But they summarily denied a stay, and that's why we're here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: And Mr. Katyal, where does this background rule come from? Is it a federal common law principle? How old is it? Do you want to talk about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0001-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress has never said the reverse."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I do think the courts have mechanisms in every circuit, and they are used, Justice Barrett, as the amici say, in every circuit for frivolous appeals to be weeded out. There's one mechanism by which, basically, the district court tells the circuit court, you know, this appeal is frivolous, give us back jurisdiction, act right away, motion to expedite or -- or sua sponte motion to expedite, and it gets thrown right back to the district court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So can you help me to understand why this is not that scenario?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Zavareei",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "If the court denies a motion for a statute of limitations or the court denies a motion for, you know, a dismissal under personal jurisdiction problems, all of these scenarios, I think, kind of have that same inherent problem."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Was that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus brief (Ninth Circuit)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0003-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under one of the amicus briefs in the Ninth Circuit, they're wrong --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Zavareei",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0003-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And in 62 percent of the times that they're wrong, Your Honor, the courts have issued stays."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Well, then should we have an automatic stay on the discretionary factors, to answer Justice Kagan's question, if discovery is about to be ordered?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 83,
        "start": 83
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: There is a possibility if we say that a stay is mandatory that we could have a situation, isn't there, where state courts could say no?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Neal K. Katyal)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0004-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Eleven times Congress affirmatively said no automatic stay during interlocutory appeals they authorized, including the very day before 16(a)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Neal K. Katyal)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And so, like, take the thousand hours we've spent in the interim in this case. If you don't get an automatic stay, attorneys will have to spend that kind of money, clients will have to spend that kind of money."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-105",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8359aba3435e4b8198b3221c34fc496b91354ef8636a3f49b0218c9e56408eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8359aba3435-0004-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 93,
        "start": 93
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
